From: Robert McFadden <robert.mcfadden@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:22:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Red Dead Redemption: the note follows the new base and the
 two rendering fixes

The movies' second audio renderer now plays through upstream's support for several renderers (A game with more than one renderer, added for Mario & Luigi: Brothership), so the note links there and the fork's own audio patch is gone. The distant blocks in the sky and the missing bodies of distant characters are resolved, with links to their entries in rendering.md; 1.0.4 was played on the Mac from a save in Armadillo.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#2005
Reason: the Red Dead Redemption note after the two rendering fixes, until upstream has the game. Goes upstream
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#999

